-- title:
--   Independence of all finite restrictions implies independence of the two real paths
-- statement:
--   The product sigma-algebra on each path space is generated by finite-coordinate cylinders. Independence of the pullbacks of every pair of such cylinders extends by the pi-lambda theorem.
-- source:
--   Kyprianou (2006), Exercise 2.8; finite-dimensional independence

